## Final answer of writer
I fixed the paging bug in `src/paginate.js`, and all 4 tests now pass.

When the item count was an exact multiple of the page size, `items.length % size` came out as 0. The last page was then sliced to zero length, so it came back empty and its items were dropped. I removed that special case, so every page is now `items.slice(start, start + size)`. `slice` already stops at the end of the array, so a partial last page still holds whatever is left.

The existing test for the multiple-of-page-size case was already failing before the change (3 of 4 passed), so I didn't add a new test. I created no scratch files, and the only modified file is `src/paginate.js`.

